+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry checks model supplied input against the same JSON Schema it advertises to providers before an executor receives the call.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- `execute` preserves an unknown tool name as a thrown `Unknown tool: <name>` error, passes schema valid input with extra properties unchanged to the executor exactly once, and returns a `ToolResponse` naming a missing required property without invoking the executor ([validated by: rejects missing required input before execution while preserving valid input and unknown names](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+- A wrong type or enum value produces a rejection result naming the failing property path and constraint; rejection results and logs never include property values, including identifying data ([validated by: rejects wrong types and enum values with paths and constraints but without input values in results or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
+- A static schema is compiled at registration, so an uncompilable schema throws there with the tool name, and the compiled schema is reused across executions ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them across ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L73)).
+- A function valued definition is resolved for each execution and input is checked against that call's schema, with validators cached by resolved schema object ([validated by: validates each function valued definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L96)).
+- A rejected tool call is returned to the model as a tool result, allowing a corrected call in a later round to complete within the configured tool round limit ([validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the provider so a corrected retry completes](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L119)).
